{"kind":"request","text":"DX-A2 contract questions from read-only preparation at Main4c333. Parent/child requests read in full; no DX-A2 source changed or tests/providers ran. Order after121a/7c0/J4 remains.\n\nThe current Head is only {seq,hash} (contract/result.ts72). ScopeApi reads route by ScopeId, whereas Receipt.fact is a FactRef with full ScopeRef/incarnation (contract/scope.ts51–65, entry.ts170). A bare Head cannot support the requested wrong-incarnation answer. I propose atLeast:number|FactRef, so receipt-aware reads forward their exact existing fact; numeric callers request position only. Please adopt that existing scoped form, or name the intended alternative.\n\nPlease define the full-fact hash condition when current seq is later than the requested seq, and when that requested position lies below the retained floor. A minimum-position wait must not silently add a new archive proof read or restore pruned payloads. Should it only require matching scope/incarnation plus seq\u003e=minimum (with followReceipt retaining its existing actual returned-entry hash check), or must it prove that exact hash belongs to the prefix? If exact prefix proof is required, name the refusal for a wrong hash or a hash no longer held.\n\nFor behind, propose adding a precise Read false variant {ok:false,reason:'behind',at:Head}, keeping existing failures unchanged. Current ReadRefusal lacks behind and its optional detail is FactRef|ScopeRef, not a bare current head. For timing propose readWaitMilliseconds=5000 in Bounds, below current card bridge10s/client30s deadlines. A waiting read keeps no storage transaction and releases the turn; existing signed-read admission charges its one real request. Please choose the active waiter bound/refusal too (suggest at most64 per scope, unavailable on saturation); a deadline alone does not cap retained waiter memory. Authorization must be rechecked before final disclosure.\n\nThe compact kit call site is browser/main.ts175–192 through ViewSessions into generic inspect→summary; the exact hosted MCP receipt read-back is hosted.ts548–553. Generic inspect cards can witness one refresh read after the act. Declared cards instead use applicationProjection, outside the four requested reads; I propose leaving that separate API out unless you explicitly extend scope. 'One request' will mean one native refresh read after the accepted act, excluding initial/pre-signing authority reads. Current wrappers call #first and may schedule existing recovery, so I propose interpreting reads-write-nothing as no journal/domain writes or new durable wait state caused by waiting, preserving existing recovery behavior; please correct if literal zero bookkeeping writes is required.","body":{"conditions":"Settle the minimum-head input/identity and full-hash/floor semantics, behind reply, bounded waiter policy and card/write-free acceptance scope before DX-A2 implementation. Source-only preparation; current121a gate and ordered7c0/J4 work continue.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}